                <pb facs="0726" n="606" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg606"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890g.6363/301: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iraq</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sloan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Baghdad</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-29T11:00:00+03:00">June 29, 1931—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 29—6:50 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>9. Information sent to the Department in my telegram 8, June 22, 10 a.m.,
                    confirmed by Minister for Foreign Affairs. Application <pb facs="0727" n="607"
                        xml:id="pg607"/> should be submitted by registered letter addressed to the
                    Minister of Economics and Communications.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sloan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
